\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Rupiah eases, Singapore dollar capped by c.bank fear\b0\par\par\uc2 673 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 August 2009\par 08:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  * Rupiah falls on dollar-covering, steady after rate cut\par \par \uc2  * Singapore dollar is seen near top end of its secret band\par \par \uc2  * Vols drop as \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears shackle Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  By Kevin Yao\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Aug 5 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah fell on Wednesday as investors took a drop in local stocks as a cue to book profits, while most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  moved in tight ranges amid worries about possible official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  Suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by some Asian central banks to curb \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation to help local exporters have driven down volatilities, with those of the Chinese yuan <CNYVOL>, Thai baht <THBVOL> and Korean won <KRWVOL> hitting multi-month lows.\par \par \uc2  RUPIAH\par \par \uc2  The rupiah <IDR=> lost 0.4 percent to 9,900 per dollar, a day after hiting its highest level since October 2008.\par \par \uc2  It was little moved after Bank Indonesia cut its policy interest rate by 25 basis points to 6.5 percent, in line with market expectations. [ID:nJAK372576].\par \par \uc2  Traders expect the rupiah to strength further.\par \par \uc2  "At this juncture, we continue to favour the rupiah on fundamental grounds," Emmanuel Ng, strategist at OCBC Bank, said in a note\par \par \uc2  The rupiah, the best performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asia, has gained just over 11 percent against the dollar so far this year, supported by a revival in risk appetite amid optimism that the the global economy is on a path of recovery.\par \par \uc2  One-month dollar/rupiah non-deliverable forwards <IDRNDFOR=> eased a tad to 9,880, implying little change from the spot. The NDFs traded 63 points below the one-month onshore forwards <IDR1M=> compared to 24 points on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2  The South Korean won <KRW=> fell slightly in step with local stocks after a 4-day rally. [ID:nSEO354145]\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar <SGD=> was stuck in a 1.4321-1.4345 range against the U.S. dollar, amid speculation that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength.\par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar has rallied 8 percent since early March, riding on fund inflows fanned by optimism about the global economy.\par \par \uc2  "I reckon investors all see that the Singapore dollar is on the stronger end of the band and are worried that the authority might be around," said a Singapore-based trader, predicing the unit would move in a range of 1.4310-1.4350 for a while.\par \par \uc2  Singapore's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  steers monetary policy by managing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within a trade-weighted band against a basket of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , rather than using interest rates.\par \par \uc2  Some analysts believe Singapore dollar's recent rally would not be sustained as the island's economy has only showed modest recovery from a deep recession.  \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day at  0617 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        94.9