\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dlr Lower Late On Weaker Stocks; Bonds Mixed\b0\par\par\uc2 345 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 August 2009\par 09:24\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                      Latest   Change \par USD/SGD              1.4346   +0.0018 \par Overnight rate        0.38%   -12 bps \par Two-year bond yield:  0.43%   -5 bps \par 10-year bond yield:   2.50%   +3 bps \par Two-year swap offer:  1.80%   +3 bps \par 10-year swap offer:   3.07%   +1 bp \par 2-10-yr swap curve:  127 bps  -2 bps \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar was lower in Asian trade late Wednesday, weighed down by weaker local stocks.\f28 \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar continued to move in a narrow range, however, trading between a high of S$1.4352 and a low of S$1.4322. OCBC strategist Selena Ling said the Singapore dollar remains on the stronger end of what is estimated to be the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore's undisclosed policy band for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which may be limiting further upside for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as well.\par \par \uc2 Three people familiar with the situation told Dow Jones Newswires Tuesday that the MAS entered the market to support the U.S. dollar around S$1.4320. One of the people said the MAS will continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  as needed.\par \par \uc2 Ling said trade in the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar has been subdued for the day.\par \par \uc2 "If you look at the STI (Straits Times Index), it's not really going anywhere," she said. "Maybe people will wait for the (U.S. economic data)."\par \par \uc2 Traders have said that the movement for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains limited given the lack of clarity on state of the global economy. The Singapore dollar has been trading mostly in narrow ranges in recent weeks, taking cues from the major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  due to a lack of domestic cues to generate momentum.\par \par \uc2 The local government bond yield curve steepened, with flows returning to the short end of the curve as overnight rates eased. Longer-dated paper were under profit-taking pressures, a trader with a foreign bank said.\par \par \uc2 -By Se Young Lee, Dow Jones Newswires; +65 6415 4155; vincent.lee@dowjones.com [ 05-08-09 0724GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1163 1859   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020090805e585000hn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
