\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Rupiah gains; baht seen capped by c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 593 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Juli 2009\par 04:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 * Rupiah rises but faces key resistance at 10,000/USD level\par \par \uc2 * Official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  suspected to contain baht strength\par \par \uc2 By Kevin Yao\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 , July 23 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah rose against the dollar on on Thursday as risk appetite improved modestly, while the Thai baht's gains sparked dollar buying by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Asian stocks looked set to test the previous day's 10-month high while the dollar hovered near a seven-week low against big \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as solid earnings from Apple and \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  offset weak bank results. [ID:nSP518702] [ID:nT264892]\par \par \uc2 RUPIAH\par \par \uc2 The high-yielding rupiah <IDR=> gained 0.3 percent to 10,050 per dollar, cementing its position as the best performer in Asia with a gain of 9.5 percent so far this year.\par \par \uc2 But traders said it faced resistance at the 10,000 level.\par \par \uc2 "There is a lot of month-end onshore dollar demand," said a Jakarta-based trader.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, one-month offshore dollar/rupiah NDFs <IDRNDFOR=> held steady at 10,070, implying little change from the spot. The one-month NDFs traded 44 points below onshore forwards <IDR1M=> compared to 53 points a day earlier.\par \par \uc2 Enrico Tanuwidjaja, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 OCBC Bank\uc2 , said the market remained bullish on the rupiah despite last week's deadly bombings in Jakarta.\par \par \uc2 "Dollar/rupiah NDFs are relatively stable, unbudged by the incident," he said. "The political outlook seems to be the key reason not to be overly jitterish about the Indonesian market."\par \par \uc2 BAHT\par \par \uc2 The baht <THB=TH> briefly rose to 33.90 per dollar before pulling back to 34, as traders suspected dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to contain the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise.\par \par \uc2 "They don't want the baht to appreciate too quickly," said a trader in Bangkok, adding that suspected dollar buying by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  occurred at levels from 33.94 to 34.\par \par \uc2 The baht has gained almost 7 percent since early March amid tentative signs of a global economic recovery, fanning concerns that a stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  may hurt exporters.\par \par \uc2 A blast near an Asian security meeting in Thailand's holiday resort Phuket had little impact on the baht, traders said. [ID:nSP490591] \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on the day at 0545 GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        94.20          93.59       -0.65\par  Sing dlr        1.4405         1.4423       +0.12\par  Taiwan dlr      32.809         32.875       +0.20\par  Korean won     1248.50        1248.00       -0.04\par  Baht             33.96          33.98       +0.06\par  Peso             48.14          48.16       +0.04\par  Rupiah        10045.00       10080.00       +0.35\par  Rupee            48.42          48.52       +0.20\par  Ringgit         3.5390         3.5510       +0.34\par  Yuan            6.8306         6.8306       +0.00\par  Change so far in 2009\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        94.20          90.60    