\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Ringgit falls, Singapore dlr eases amid cbank fear\b0\par\par\uc2 653 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Juli 2009\par 08:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Ringgit falls on broad dollar strength\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar eases amid \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  jitters\par \par \uc2 By Kevin Yao\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 , July 1 (Reuters) - The Malaysian ringgit fell against a broadly firmer dollar on Wednesday, while the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar eased as investors fretted about possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength.\par \par \uc2 The dollar stayed firm against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  after gaining on safe-haven bids the previous session after an unexpected fall in U.S. consumer confidence cooled optimism about an economic recovery. [ID:nT146254]\par \par \uc2 Trading was lacklustre with Thailand's markets closed for holiday.\par \par \uc2 RINGGIT\par \par \uc2 The Malaysian ringgit <MYR=> fell 0.4 percent to 3.5260 per dollar, pressured by the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's broad strength.\par \par \uc2 "Overnight euro softness on dollar short covering made dollar/ringgit biddish," said a trader in Kuala Lumpur.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday the ringgit hit its highest since mid-June after Prime Minister Najib Razak unveiled steps to attract foreign investment.\par \par \uc2 Some analysts suspect Malaysia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , or BNM, may have been trying to weaken the ringgit to help exporters as its rate-cutting cycle draws to an end.\par \par \uc2 "We think BNM used dollar weakness to accommodate ringgit depreciation pressure and this explains the move in the Singapore dollar/ringgit cross rate earlier this month above its long-term 2.38-2.42 trading range," analysts at ING said in a note.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  "In view of the policy constraints -- BNM's easing cycle is\par over and there will be no more fiscal packages -- we expect\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore dollar/ringgit to remain above 2.42 for the rest of the year," they added.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The ringgit eased to 2.4316 against the Singapore dollar <SGDMYR=R> from Tuesday's close at 2.4216.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE DOLLAR\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Singapore dollar <SGD=> shed a fifth of a percent to 1.4505 per U.S. dollar amid fears that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stem the local unit's strength.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The jitters are always there," said a trader in Singapore.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Singapore dollar has gained 7 percent since early March, fanned by tentative signs of a recovery in the global economy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In April, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  eased policy by lowering the mid-point of the undisclosed \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  band to help the economy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sean Callow, strategist at Westpac, estimates Singapore dollar's recent rise had yet to upset the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as its nominal effective exchange rate was still within the band.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We see Singapore dollar at about 1.48 over the month ahead, though this is a U.S. dollar story," he said in a note. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day at  0631 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highli