\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Rupiah jumps on risk appetite, Singapore dollar up\b0\par\par\uc2 611 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juni 2009\par 07:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Rupiah jumps on renewed interest in high-yielding assets\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar edges up despite \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears\par \par \uc2 By Kevin Yao\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 , June 26 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah jumped on Friday as investors bought risky assets after the Federal Reserve signalled a day earlier it would keep interest rates low, while other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  moved in thin ranges in lacklustre trade.\par \par \uc2 Asian stocks firmed following a rise on Wall Street on Thursday, while the dollar fell against a basket of major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  <.DXY>, extending losses made the previous day as investors shifted funds back to riskier assets offering the potential for higher yields. [ID:nT314363]\par \par \uc2 RUPIAH\par \par \uc2 The Indonesian rupiah <IDR=> jumped just over 1 percent to 10,130 per dollar as investors bought local assets.\par \par \uc2 "Offshore investors are coming back," said a Jakarta-based trader.\par \par \uc2 Market players expected the rupiah to benefit from further interest rate cuts as inflation falls, which may boost local stocks and bonds, traders said.\par \par \uc2 But the chart shows the rupiah faces near-term resistance at 10,000.\par \par \uc2 The offshore dollar/rupiah non-deliverable forwards curve shifted lower, but failed to match the spot's move.\par \par \uc2 Six-month dollar/rupiah NDFs <IDR6MNDFOR=> dipped to 10,447, implying a 3.3 percent rupiah fall from the spot compared to 3.0 percent on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The six-month NDFs traded 100 points below onshore forwards <IDR6M=> with the same tenor, little changed from in the previous day.\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar <SGD=> gained a fifth of a percent to 1.4542 per U.S. dollar, tracking the euro's gains against the U.S. dollar <EUR=>.\par \par \uc2 It showed little reaction to data showing Singapore's May factory output fell 1.6 percent from April on a seasonally adjusted basis but still rose 2 percent from a year earlier. [ID:nSGC001194]\par \par \uc2 "The U.S. dollar's downside against Singapore dollar is limited, while its upside is also limited as some people want to sell U.S. dollar as Singapore dollar is perpetually viewed as a safe-haven \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said a trader in Singapore.\par \par \uc2 Sentiment remained cautious as many players in the market believed the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was close to the upper end of its trade-weighted band, making it vulnerable to possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb its strength. \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day at  0547 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        95.88          95.90       +0.02\par  Sing dlr        1.4553         1.4574       +0.14\par  Taiwan dlr      32.929         32.970       +0.12\par  Korean won     1286.40        1288.80       +0.19\par  Baht             34.07          34.11       +0.12\par  Peso             48.32          48.35       +0.07\par  Rupiah        10160.00       10260.00       +0.98\par  Rupee            48.54          48.59       +0.10\par  Ringgit         3.5365         3.5340       -0.07\par  Yuan            6.8349         6.8347       -0.00\par  Change so far in 2009\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev