\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Peso dips,  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  dlr up despite  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  fear\b0\par\par\uc2 669 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juni 2009\par 08:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Peso extends losses as investors take dim view on economy\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar rises but capped by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears\par \par \uc2 By Kevin Yao\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 , June 18 (Reuters) - The Philippine peso extended recent losses on Thursday on heightened concerns about the health of the economy, while the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar's rise fuelled fears of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The dollar steadied against the euro <EUR=>, hovering near lows struck the previous day after tame U.S. inflation data further dampened speculation the Federal Reserve would raise interest rates any time soon. [ID:nT27037]\par \par \uc2 PESO\par \par \uc2 The Philippine peso <PHP=> lost a third of a percent to 48.50 per dollar, its lowest since April 30, as investors dumped local stocks amid worries about the economy.\par \par \uc2 "Sentiment is still very negative for the Philippine economy in the short term as epitomised by the weakness of the stock market," said a Manila-based trader.\par \par \uc2 The Philippines recorded a balance of payments deficit in May, the second monthly shortfall this year, on higher external debt payments by the government and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . [ID:nMAN217523]\par \par \uc2 On the chart, dollar/peso faced some resistance at 48.57 and the break of that could take the pair to 48.70, traders said. Meanwhile, three-month dollar/peso NDFs <PHPNDFOR=> steady at 49.02, implying a 1.2 percent peso fall from the spot compared to 1.7 percent on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The peso has been hurt in recent weeks by concerns about the country's economic outlook and a widening budget deficit as the government ratchet up spending to support growth.\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar <SGD=> edged up to 1.4515 per U.S. dollar -- its highest in nearly a week -- taking its cue from the euro's rise against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 But the gain was limited on jitters of official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap its strength.\par \par \uc2 "It's all euro driven," said a Singapore-based trader, referring \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar's rise.\par \par \uc2 Some traders fretted about \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as they believed the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar had risen to the firmer end of its undisclosed band.\par \par \uc2 But Westpac strategist Sean Callow said he reckoned the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  let the local unit move at least 2 percent up or down from the mid-point within the band, which indicated little urgency for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "I agree it's on the stronger side of the band but is not close to the edge," he said.\par \par \uc2 Singapore's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  manages the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within a trade-weighted band to steer monetary policy. In April, it eased policy by lowering the mid-point of the band to support the recession-hit economy. \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on the day at 0616 GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        95.77          95.69 