\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dlr Higher Late As Regional Stocks Rise; Bonds Up\b0\par\par\uc2 328 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Juni 2009\par 09:46\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                          Latest   Change \par    USD/SGD              1.4353   -0.0077 \par    Overnight rate        0.31%    +25 bps \par    Two-year bond yield:  0.41%    -12 bps \par    10-year bond yield:   2.59%    -8 bps \par    Two-year swap offer:  1.67%     Unchanged \par    10-year swap offer:   2.99%    -9 bps \par    2-10-yr swap curve:   132 bps  -9 bps \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar was higher in Asian trade late Wednesday, in line with regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on stronger equity markets.\f28 \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar traded as low as S$1.4340, as it hit a seven-month low against the pound and an eight-month low against the Australian dollar.\par \par \uc2 "Recent economic data are fitting into either the good or great category. There are no bad numbers," \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2  said in a report. "Risk appetite is once again in the ascendancy as investors are cheered by data."\par \par \uc2 Nevertheless, the Singapore dollar's gains were relatively moderate during the Asian session, locked in a relatively narrow range against the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 Traders have said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  several times in May to try to slow the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise, leading to caution among investors. A person familiar with the situation told Dow Jones Newswires Tuesday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  propped up the greenback around S$1.4382.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  uses the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as its chief policy tool, managing it in an undisclosed trade-weighted band. With the economy in a severe recession, a stronger Singapore dollar could delay recovery for the export-dependent city state that has been devastated by a sharp decline in external demand.\par \par \uc2 Local government bonds made strong gains on the back of firmer U.S. Treasurys. A rise in the Singapore dollar typically provides support to the market.\par \par \uc2 -By Se Young Lee, Dow Jones Newswires; +65 6415 4155; vincent.lee@dowjones.com [ 03-06-09 0746GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1163 1859   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020090603e5630008z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
