\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Rangebound,  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  dlr capped by  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  fear\b0\par\par\uc2 597 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Mai 2009\par 06:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar rises but contained by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fear\par \par \uc2  * Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  move in narrow ranges in line with stocks\par \par \uc2  By Kevin Yao\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, May 29 (Reuters) - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  moved in thin ranges on Friday in tandem with regional stock markets on uncertainties about the global economy, with gains in the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar sparking fears of official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  The Japanese yen firmed against the dollar <JPY=>, buoyed by the biggest monthly spike in Japanese industrial output since 1953, but a top Federal Reserve official said the U.S. economy will not recover in a "meaningful" way before the end of this year. [ID:nT14122] [ID:nN28511844].\par \par \uc2  Trading activity remained lacklustre with markets in China and Taiwan closed for holdays.\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar <SGD=> gained a fifth of a percent to 1.45 per U.S. dollar but investors treaded cautiously amid fears of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to contain the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's advance.\par \par \uc2  "The 1.45 level has to hold, if it breaks then the next support should be 1.4460-1.4470," said a trader in Singapore.\par \par \uc2  Some traders suspected the authority bought U.S. dollars at 1.4505-1.4510 on Thursday.\par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar has gained 7 percent since early March due to tentative signs of a global economic recovery, but analysts say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's tolerance may be tested if it rises further.\par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  eased monetary policy in April by lowering the mid-point \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's trade-weighted undisclosed band to help the recession-hit economy.\par \par \uc2  PESO\par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso <PHP=> moved between 47.37-47.58 per dollar compared to Thursday's close at 47.46, as investor sentiment was caught between firmer local stocks <.PSI> and concerns about the country's economic outlook.\par \par \uc2  "Domestic growth concerns are keeping dollar/peso supported after yesterday's downward revision to 2008 GDP figures and the unexpectedly weak first-quarter GDP," said a trader in Manila.\par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut its key interest rate by 25 basis points on Thursday and said there was room for further cuts to try to head off a recession.\par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, three-month offshore non-deliverable forwards <PHPNDFOR=> edged up to 47.84, implying a 0.7 percent peso fall from the spot compared to 1.2 percent on Thursday.  \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day at   0352 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        96.32          96.94       +0.64\par  Sing dlr        1.4498         1.4525       +0.19\par  Korean won     1260.70        1256.90       -0.30\par  Baht             34.35          34.40       +0.15\par  Peso             47.49          47.46       -0.06\par  Rupiah        10330.00       10300.00       -0.29\par  Rupee            47.53          47.60       +0.15\par  Ringgit         3.5050         3.5100       +0.14\par  Change so far in 2009\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        96.32          90.60       -5.94\par  Sing dlr        1.4498         1.4340       -1.09\par  Taiwan dlr      32.620         32.860       +0.74\par  Korean won     1260.70        1259.50       -0.10\par  Baht             34.35          34.80       +1.31\par  Peso             47.49          47.52       +0.06\par  Rupiah        10330.00       11000.00       +6.49\par  Rupee            47.53          48.71       +2.48\par  Ringgit         3.5050         3.4500       -1.57\par  Yuan            6.8279         6.8230       -0.07\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  (Reporting by Kevin Yao; Editing by Kim Coghill)\par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ASIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|IF|PHD|SI|Z|J|SNS|SNI|RNP|DNP|PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090601e55t00074\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
