\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 735 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Mai 2009\par 07:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: SINGAPORE 1Q GDP -14.6% ON QTR;ECON MAY BE BOTTOMING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A senior government official said Thursday that Singapore's economy is showing signs of bottoming as it contracted at a slower pace than initially estimated during the first quarter of the year. (published 0137 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  WANTS US DLR OVER S$1.45; MORE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  -SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities want the U.S. dollar to stay above S$1.45 and will continue \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to smooth the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar's rise, a person familiar with the matter said Thursday. (published 0338 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par MAS: COMFORTABLE WITH CURRENT SINGAPORE DLR POLICY BAND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Singapore \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  remains comfortable with its undisclosed policy band to manage the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  despite its recent gains against the U.S. dollar, a senior official said Thursday. (published 0108 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par TAIWAN 1Q GDP FALLS AROUND 10% ON YEAR - PANEL MEMBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Taiwan's economy contracted around 10% from a year earlier in the first quarter, a senior member of the island's gross domestic product review panel told Dow Jones Newswires Thursday. (published 0326 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par HKMA YAM:DON'T SEE HKD/USD PEG CHANGING IN FORESEEABLE FUTURE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hong Kong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Chief Executive Joseph Yam said Thursday he doesn't see Hong Kong's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  peg to the U.S. dollar changing in the foreseeable future. (published 0318 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA OVERSEAS DEBT DECLINES FOR 2ND STRAIGHT QUARTER IN 1Q \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's overseas debt fell for the second straight quarter in the first quarter due to a decline in banks' external borrowing, Bank of Korea data showed Thursday. (published 0300 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par GEITHNER: WITH TARP REPAYMENTS, TREASURY CAN OFFER 'NEW' AID \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Treasury Secretary Timothy Geithner told a U.S. senator Wednesday that the department's plan to reopen the $700 billion Troubled Asset Relief Program to small banks isn't exactly recycling. (published 2237 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =3RD UPDATE: FED MAY NEED TO BUY MORE TREASURYS, MBS - MINUTES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve officials Wednesday opened the door to raising the amounts of mortgage-related and Treasury securities purchases beyond the $1.75 trillion they've already committed to buying. (published 1928 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BOK: LIQUIDITY SUPPLIED TO FINCL MARKET DEEMED NOT EXCESSIVE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Korea said Thursday that it judges the financial market to have abundant short-term liquidity as a result of monetary easing, but that money supply isn't excessive. (published 0125 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =OMB CHIEF: NO SIGN OF SLUMPING DEMAND FOR US TREASURY DEBT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 There's no indication that foreign investors are losing their appetite for U.S. government debt, Office of Management and Budget Director Peter Orszag said Wednesday. (published 2229 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par =MONEY TALKS: THAILAND RISKS OVERRELIANCE ON FISCAL HELP \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thai authorities will be relying more on government spending than interest rates to do the heavy lifting for the economy from now on, but when it comes to the fiscal side of things there's not much wriggle room. (published 0001 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =PREVIEW: MALAYSIA CTRL BK LIKELY TO KEEP POLICY RATE AT 2.0% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will keep its benchmark overnight policy rate unchanged Tuesday despite an anemic economic outlook, economists said. (published 0216 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =INDIA RUPEE LIKELY SOFT IN FORWARDS MKT ON OIL, EXPORT WOES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Indian rupee is likely to weaken in the forwards market as declining exports and rising crude-oil prices are expected to subdue the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's recent surge induced by the federal-election results, analysts said. (published 0400 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =OFF THE RUN: A NEW NORM FOR INTERBANK LENDING MARKETS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The interbank lending market has improved by leaps and bounds since last fall when lending rates spiked and risk gauges ballooned as concerns about counterparty risk intensified in the wake of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Lehman Brothers\f28 \uc2 \f2  bankruptcy. (published 2021 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =FED WATCH: CAUTION A GOOD IDEA ON FUTURE FED DEBT BUYING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Economists are warning bond investors not to get carried away by news the Federal Reserve is thinking about boosting its future purchases of Treasury and mortgage debt. (published 2009 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =MUNI WATCH: WALL STREET SAYS DON'T BET AGAINST CALIFORNIA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 While California Gov. Arnold Schwarzenegger suffered a body blow from the failure of budget-related ballot measures to pass muster with fed-up voters, Wall Street is sending a clear message not to bet against the Golden State. (published 2107 GMT) [ 21-05-09 0500GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020090521e55l0003z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
