\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dlr Slightly Lower Late; Bonds Tad Higher\b0\par\par\uc2 414 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Mai 2009\par 10:47\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                          Latest   Change \par    USD/SGD              1.4701   +0.0033 \par    Overnight rate        0.19%   +6 bps \par    Two-year bond yield:  0.44%   -3 bps \par    10-year bond yield:   2.10%   -1 bp \par    Two-year swap offer:  1.57%   -4 bps \par    10-year swap offer:   2.71%    Unchanged \par    2-10-yr swap curve:  114 bps  +4 bpd \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar was slightly lower in Asian trade late Monday, as the greenback's strength from the end of the previous week carried over into the session.\f28 \par \par \uc2 But the U.S. dollar gradually gave up its gains as it slipped against some regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , trading as low as S$1.4689 as the session wore on.\par \par \uc2 Weaker-than-expected Singapore April non-oil domestic exports appeared to have little effect on trading levels, as market watchers don't expect a significant improvement in external demand until the second half of the year.\par \par \uc2 But analysts said the 19.2% on-year decline in April - worse than the 18.6% decline expected in a Dow Jones poll, and than the 17.3% fall in March - may signal that Singapore's economy will recover gradually.\par \par \uc2 "Perhaps the worst of the contraction may be behind us, but in terms of the headline numbers it's not really looking like we're on track for any meaningful V-shaped recovery," \uc2 CIMB\uc2 -GK economist Song Seng Wun said.\par \par \uc2 The local dollar has strengthened in recent weeks amid growing hopes the economy may have bottomed out and will start to recover. But any emerging risk appetite was restrained last week by signs of weakness in the equities market.\par \par \uc2 And on Monday, a person familiar with the situation said the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore will buy the U.S. dollar if it falls convincingly below S$1.46 to protect the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's undisclosed policy band, and this could restrain near-term gains in the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at least three times this month to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy band, the person said.\par \par \uc2 Local government bonds rose slightly after a weak start from local stocks and low overnight rates. But traders said movements will remain muted as players await the announcement of the size of the new 10-year bond auction, likely due later this week.\par \par \uc2 -By Se Young Lee, Dow Jones Newswires; 65 6415 4155; vincent.lee@dowjones.com [ 18-05-09 0847GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1163 1859   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020090518e55i000cn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
