\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Asia mostly weaker on profit-taking but won jumps\b0\par\par\uc2 751 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2009\par 07:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Rupiah dips as investors book profits from its recent rally\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar falls but supported by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  talk\par \par \uc2 * Yuan steady despite modest appreciation implied by NDFs\par \par \uc2 * Won jumps to two-month high on dollar stop losses\par \par \uc2 By Kevin Yao\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, March 25 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  retreated on Wednesday as investors took profits from their recent rallies, with the high-yielding Indonesian rupiah suffering sharp losses in both spot and offshore forwards.\par \par \uc2 The rupiah <IDR=> slid just over 1 percent to 11,590 per dollar, down from its two-month high hit on Tuesday fanned by the U.S. government's plan to purge toxic bank assets from banks.\par \par \uc2 "There has been some profit-taking and the majors are also retreating a bit against the dollar," said a Jakarta-based trader.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, one-year offshore dollar/rupiah non-deliverable forwards <IDR1YNDFOR=> jumped about 2.5 percent to 13,000, implying an 11 percent depreciation from the spot.\par \par \uc2 The Thai baht <THB=TH> lost 0.7 percent to 35.60 per dollar at one point, but later pulled back to 35.50.\par \par \uc2 "The baht moves lower in line with regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The dollar/baht should meet resistance at 35.50 and 35.83 respectively," said a trader in Bangkok.\par \par \uc2 The baht is still up nearly 2 percent this month as part of an Asia-wide rally fuelled by optimism that the global financial system may be stabilising and the dollar's broad retreat against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar <SGD=> shed a third of a percent to 1.5177 to the U.S. dollar as investors moved to cover their short U.S. dollar positions, but it later pared losses amid talk of possible official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Traders reckon the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar is near the bottom of its secret trade-weighted band which is widely expected to be shifted lower when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reviews policy in early April.\par \par \uc2 "We see no convincing argument against a loosening of monetary policy at the April review," Sean Callow, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Westpac, said in a note.\par \par \uc2 "Unlike most economies, its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is Singapore's policy instrument so there is no question of 'beggar thy neighbour' policy," he said.\par \par \uc2 The Chinese yuan <CNY=CFXS> was little changed at 6.832 per dollar, while one-year offshore dollar/yuan NDFs <CNYNDFOR=> rose slightly to 6.80, implying a 0.5 percent rise from the spot.\par \par \uc2 "We remain convinced that 'basic stability' will be maintained in the exchange rate," Patrick Bennett, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Societe Generale, said in a note.\par \par \uc2 Using the NDF to hedge China investment or exposure at current levels in still uncertain times is an appropriate move," he added.\par \par \uc2 The South Korean won <KRW=> hit a two-month high of 1,357.9 per dollar, bucking regional weakness as investors who were long on U.S. dollars rushed to dump the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on stop-losses.\par \par \uc2 Traders said stop-losses in closing trader were triggered by heavy dollar sales by exporters and talk of POSCO converting its dollar bond proceeds.\par \par \uc2 "Equities inflows triggered stops below the previous low. Technically we can see it rising to 1,350," said a trader in Singapore. \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on the day at 0607 GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        97.64          97.75       +0.11\par  Sing dlr        1.5124         1.5125       +0.01\par  Taiwan dlr      33.895         33.788       -0.32\par  Korean won     1361.50        1383.50       +1.62\par  Baht             35.51          35.36       -0.42\par  Peso             48.25          48.24       -0.02\par  Rupiah        11550.00       11450.00       -0.87\par  Rupee            50.90          50.71       -0.37\par  Ringgit         3.6260         3.6230       -0.08\par  Yuan            6.8317         6.8296       -0.03\par  Change so far in 2009\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        97.64          90.60       -7.21\par  Sing dlr        1.5124         1.4340       -5.18\par  Taiwan dlr      33.895         32.860       -3.05\par  Korean won     1361.50        1259.50       -7.49\par  Baht             35.51          34.80       -2.00\par  Peso             48.25          47.52       -1.51\par  Rupiah        11550.00       11000.00       -4.76\par  Rupee            50.90          48.71       -4.30\par  Ringgit         3.6260         3.4500       -4.85\par  Yuan            6.8317         6.8230       -0.13\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Reporting by Kevin Yao; Editing by Kim Coghill)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ASIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|IF|PHD|SI|Z|J|SNS|SNI|RNP|DNP|PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090328e53p0003y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
