\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dlr Lower Late On Risk Aversion; Bonds Fall\b0\par\par\uc2 336 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Februar 2009\par 08:33\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                          Latest   Change \par    USD/SGD              1.5149   +0.0074 \par    Overnight rate        0.25%    Unchanged \par    Two-year bond yield:  0.76%   +2 bps \par    10-year bond yield:   2.14%   +7 bps \par    Two-year swap offer:  1.56%   +6 bps \par    10-year swap offer:   2.50%   +8 bps \par    2-10-yr swap curve:   94 bps  +2 bps \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar was lower for a third consecutive Asian session late Monday, as continuing risk aversion pressured the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  lower.\f28 \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar traded in a relatively narrow range, moving from an intraday high of S$1.5177 to a low of S$1.5096.\par \par \uc2 "The market wants to buy U.S. dollar, but there are worries about a possible \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on and off, so investors are a little cautious," said a trader with a foreign bank.\par \par \uc2 Analysts say the MAS, which uses the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as its chief policy tool and manages it in an undisclosed trading band, has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market in the past to reduce volatility in the Singapore dollar.\par \par \uc2 Some market watchers estimate that the Singapore dollar has ventured closer to the floor of the policy band, raising concerns that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will step in.\par \par \uc2 But the fundamental outlook for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains negative, given the deteriorating macroeconomic conditions. Standard Chartered said in a report that real money funds continue to build up long positions on the U.S. dollar against the Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  excluding the Japanese yen.\par \par \uc2 Local government bonds fell across the board, as the yield curve steepened on stronger selling pressure on the long-term notes due to a fresh supply of 20-year bonds to be auctioned later this month. Short-term paper retained some support on the low overnight rate and investors seeking safe haven assets.\par \par \uc2 -By Se Young Lee, Dow Jones Newswires; 65 6415 4155; vincent.lee@dowjones.com [ 02-02-09 0733GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1163 1859   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020090202e522000bx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
