\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dlr Lower Late On Risk Aversion, Glum Econ Outlook\b0\par\par\uc2 346 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Dezember 2008\par 08:17\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                          Latest   Change \par    USD/SGD              1.5307   +0.0101 \par    Overnight rate        0.50%   -13 bps \par    Two-year bond yield:  0.81%    Unchanged \par    10-year bond yield:   2.20%   -4 bps \par    Two-year swap offer:  1.62%   -5 bps \par    10-year swap offer:   2.40%   -9 bps \par    2-10-yr swap curve:  78 bps   -4 bps \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar was lower in Asian trade late Tuesday, tracking regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as heightened risk aversion continued to push the greenback higher.\f28 \par \par \uc2 But the U.S. dollar's moves were relatively modest, trading from an intraday high of S$1.5315 to a low of S$1.5269. Traders said there were no major news to drive the market, and that Wall Street's overnight plunge virtually assured a weak day for regional bourses.\par \par \uc2 Still, traders say there's little relief in sight for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . With the economy already in a recession and external demand unlikely to recover anytime soon, they say there is very little incentive for the market to buy into the Singapore dollar.\par \par \uc2 "I don't think the (\b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  (soon) to stop the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar's fall, unless it is much faster than they expect," said a strategist with a local bank.\par \par \uc2 Many economists also believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will ease policy prior to its next semiannual meeting in April to support the economy. MAS, which uses the Singapore dollar as its chief policy tool and manages it in an undisclosed band, shifted to a neutral policy in October and can either re-center the midpoint of the band downward or widen the width of the band to allow the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken further.\par \par \uc2 Local government bonds were mixed, traders said, with long-term papers gaining on higher risk aversion while the weakening Singapore dollar and already strong valuation kept the short-term bonds flat.\par \par \uc2 -By Se Young Lee, Dow Jones Newswires; 65 6415 4155; vincent.lee@dowjones.com [ 02-12-08 0717GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1163 1859   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020081202e4c20008d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
