\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dlr Higher Late Tue; FOMC's Rate Decision In Focus\b0\par\par\uc2 309 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Oktober 2008\par 08:12\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                         Latest    Change \par    USD/SGD              1.5041    -0.0014 \par    Overnight rate        0.75%    +20 bps \par    Two-year bond yield:  1.15%    +2 bps \par    10-year bond yield:   2.97%    +13 bps \par    Two-year swap offer:  2.33%    +20 bps \par    10-year swap offer:   3.42%    +17 bps \par    2-10-yr swap curve:  109 bps   -3 bps \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar was higher in Asian trade Tuesday, buoyed by rallying Asian equities and market players taking profit from recent U.S. dollar strength ahead of the Federal Open Market Committee's meeting.\f28 \par \par \uc2 The greenback rose as high as S$1.5143 in early trade, but gave up its gains as the session wore on. Three traders told Dow Jones Newswires that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  likely \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to stem the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's slide.\par \par \uc2 "Looking at the price action, it is sure that they (the MAS) are in," a trader with a foreign bank said.\par \par \uc2 "This is part of a process various central banks are taking to support their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," another trader with a local bank said.\par \par \uc2 OCBC Strategist Selena Ling said the market seems to be consolidating, as some players repositioned, with the market having priced in a 50-basis-point rate cut by the FOMC. The FOMC will meet later Tuesday for a two-day meeting.\par \par \uc2 "People may be adjusting on the possibility of the Fed moving more than expected," she added.\par \par \uc2 Local government bonds fell across the board with players repositioning as regional equities rose, traders said. But the short-end bonds were better supported as the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gained against the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 -By Se Young Lee, Dow Jones Newswires; 65 6415 4155; vincent.lee@dowjones.com [ 28-10-08 0712GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1163 1859   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020081028e4as000eq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
