\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  Dlr Lowest Since Jan; \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Fears To Cap Fall\b0\par\par\uc2 474 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 September 2008\par 10:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                          Latest   Change \par    USD/SGD               1.4433  +0.0131 \par    Overnight rate        1.00%    Unchanged \par    Two-year bond yield:  1.44%   +1 bp \par    10-year bond yield:   3.11%   +1 bp \par    Two-year swap offer:  2.23%   +1 bp \par    10-year swap offer:   3.27%    Unchanged \par    2-10-yr swap curve:   104 bps -1 bp \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar sank to a new eight-month low in Asian trade Thursday on broad strength in the greenback, despite talk that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  early in the session to slow the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's fall.\f28 \par \par \uc2 "We saw this morning a high of around S$1.4420 for the U.S. dollar, then saw it drop all the way to S$1.4350," said a strategist with a local bank. "That's being attributed to official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 The strategist added that, judging from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar's movements in recent sessions, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore has likely been entering the market to smoothen the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's slide. She estimated that the MAS may have spent as much as US$1 billion so far this week.\par \par \uc2 "Looking at where (the Singapore dollar) is trading now, it's likely that they have to come in," a trader with a foreign bank said. "They're just trying to smoothen out the market."\par \par \uc2 The MAS uses the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as its policy tool, managing it in an undisclosed policy band.\par \par \uc2 The MAS's style "is not to try to change the market direction but more to try to smoothen the move," the strategist said. "They probably don't want to see (the levels) move more than one big figure a day."\par \par \uc2 But the respite offered by the suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was short-lived, as the U.S. dollar rose to S$1.4433 - its highest since January - as it extended gains against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 After retreating Monday in the wake of the U.S. government's bailout of \uc2 Freddie Mac\uc2  and \uc2 Fannie Mae\uc2 , the greenback has regained momentum on a deteriorating global economic growth outlook. The U.S. dollar traded at S$1.4170 in Asia late Monday, then rose back to S$1.4326 by late Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Traders said the greenback is likely to remain strong against Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but added that the market's wariness over the MAS's suspected intention to limit the Singapore dollar's fall will likely keep its slide relatively gradual.\par \par \uc2 Local government bonds fell slightly, but traders said the market was muted given the lack of major cues and as investors continue to assess the impact of the \uc2 Freddie Mac\uc2  and \uc2 Fannie Mae\uc2  bailout on U.S. Treasurys.\par \par \uc2 -By Se Young Lee, Dow Jones Newswires; 65 6415 4155; vincent.lee@dowjones.com [ 11-09-08 0801GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1163 1859   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020080911e49b000bv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
