\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore dollar's volatilities jump as spot rate rises\b0\par\par\uc2 523 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Juli 2008\par 11:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, July 17 (Reuters) - Implied volatilities on the Singapore dollar jumped higher as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit a record high this week, but analysts caution that the authorities would prevent sharp \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains even as they try to quell inflation.\par \par \uc2 One-month implied volatilities <SGDVOL> reached as high as 5.0 percent on Wednesday, the strongest level since June 27. They eased a tad to 4.8 percent on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, the volatilities registered their sharpest daily percentage gain in three years, when the Singapore dollar <SGD=> hit a record high at 1.3453 against the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 Rising implied volatilities, a measure of how much the market expects the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to move, indicate the options market expects the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will become increasingly volatile.\par \par \uc2 Traders said investors rushed to buy protection through options to hedge against further falls in the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 "The Singapore dollar's volatilities were begging for a retrace given that they had come off significantly since June," said Emmanuel Ng, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 OCBC Bank.\par \par \uc2 "Implied option skews had moved to uncharacteristically favour U.S. dollar calls, but in the past few sessions the downward move in the U.S. dollar versus Singapore dollar has 'corrected' the skews," Ng said.\par \par \uc2 The volatilities had been falling since it hit as high as 6.8 percent in early June.\par \par \uc2 Investors have significantly increased their long positions in the Singapore dollar in the first half of July as they expect the authorities to tolerate further \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rises to help fight inflation, a Reuters poll showed. [ID:nSP231499]\par \par \uc2 But analysts sounded a cautious note, predicting Singapore's authorities would try to prevent any sharp move in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which would hit exports and in turn weigh on the economy.\par \par \uc2 "I think the market needs to be a little bit cautious in taking this \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  too far. If it rises beyond 1.3450, I think it will face strong resistance from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Joseph Tan, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Fortis.\par \par \uc2 "As long as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's move is on a very gradual basis, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is OK with that, but any volatile move will be met with \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he added.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has gained 2 percent since June 13, despite frequent dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MAS).\par \par \uc2 In April, the MAS shifted the centre of its trading band upwards to try to quell inflation, but it's widely expected to keep policy steady in October and refrain from tightening further.\par \par \uc2 Consumer prices in May gained 7.5 percent from a year earlier, keeping inflation at a 26-year high struck the month before.\par \par \uc2 The export-dependent economy shrank at an annualised and seasonally adjusted rate of 6.6 percent in the second quarter -- the sharpest contraction in five years.\par \par \uc2 Singapore's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  conducts monetary policy by managing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within a secret trading band against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  instead of setting interest rates. (Reporting by Kevin Yao; editing by Neil Fullick)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-SINGAPORE/DOLLAR|LANGEN|ABN|M|SI|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080717e47h000pz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
