\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore dlr hits record high on flows, stop losses\b0\par\par\uc2 223 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juli 2008\par 10:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, July 15 (Reuters) - The Singapore dollar jumped to a record high against a broadly weaker U.S. dollar on Tuesday, buoyed by technical factors and flows into an economy perceived to be a safe haven as financial sector concerns mount elsewhere. The Singapore dollar <SGD=> inched up by 0.6 percent on Tuesday to hit 1.3465 per U.S. dollar, strengthening past the previous record high of 1.3468 per dollar touched on April 23.\par \par \uc2 "Investment banks are the main sellers of U.S. dollars," one trader in Singapore said.\par \par \uc2 Another trader said heavy stop-losses were triggered as the U.S. dollar weakened on the back of the U.S. government's bailout plan for the country's two big mortgage lenders, causing more sales of U.S. dollars around the 1.3470 level against the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 This trader suspected the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has gained 6.8 percent so far this year while some others, such as the South Korean won <KRW=>, have been hit by soaring oil prices <CLc1> and fears of slowing growth.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Melissa Chia; Editing by Jacqueline Wong)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-SINGAPORE/DOLLAR (URGENT)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|PHD|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080715e47f000sa\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
