\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dlr Higher Late Mon, Gains Capped; Bonds Higher\b0\par\par\uc2 363 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Juni 2008\par 10:56\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                          Latest   Change \par    USD/SGD               1.3627  -0.0032 \par    Overnight rate        0.19%   -31 bps \par    Two-year bond yield:  1.08%   -12 bps \par    10-year bond yield:   3.19%   -32 bps \par    Two-year swap offer:  2.47%   -6 bps \par    10-year swap offer:   3.74%   -7 bps \par    2-10-yr swap curve:   127 bps -1 bp \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar was higher in Asian trade late Monday, but gains were capped as its relative strength against the U.S. dollar raised concerns about a possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 A strategist with a foreign bank said the early morning levels were on the "extreme strong" end of his estimates of the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's undisclosed policy band for managing the local unit. The MAS' preference to avoid excessive swings for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in turn made traders more cautious, he said.\par \par \uc2 "At this point, it's pretty difficult to short the (U.S.) dollar against the Singapore dollar," the strategist said. "If anything, you look at it and say 'Hey, why don't we go long?'"\par \par \uc2 Another trader noted that levels have stabilized during the afternoon, with no clear impetus to move for or against the local unit.\par \par \uc2 Market watchers said trading levels in the short term are likely to depend on whether the recent fall in crude oil prices will continue and how inflationary pressures will affect the growth of Asian economies.\par \par \uc2 The strategist said that while regional central banks want to fight rising oil and food prices with a stronger local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , signs of weakening economic growth are starting to slow the capital inflows that could be used to prop their respective monetary units.\par \par \uc2 "Inflation is getting pretty ugly, and the fact that lead indicators are pointing to deteriorating growth makes it hard to get too excited about Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said.\par \par \uc2 Local government bonds jumped during the session in a market flush with liquidity and players short-covering after the selloff in recent sessions, traders said.\par \par \uc2 -By Se Young Lee, Dow Jones Newswires; 65 6415 4155; vincent.lee@dowjones.com [ 02-06-08 0856GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1163 1859   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020080602e462000en\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
