\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dlr Higher Late Fri; Uncertainty On New Top Of Band\b0\par\par\uc2 368 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 April 2008\par 09:16\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                          Latest   Change \par    USD/SGD              1.3572   -0.0023 \par    Overnight rate        0.56%    Unchanged \par    Two-year bond yield:  0.83%   +3 bps \par    10-year bond yield:   2.30%   +3 bps \par    Two-year swap offer:  1.83%   +5 bps \par    10-year swap offer:   3.09%   Unchanged \par    2-10-yr swap curve:   126 bps -5 bps \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar was slightly higher in Asian trade late Friday, but traders said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was locked in a tight range with investors cashing out after Thursday's major gains against the greenback.\f28 \par \par \uc2 Traders said the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to continue appreciating against the U.S. dollar in the near term, after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore surprised the market Thursday by tightening its monetary policy by re-centering its undisclosed trading band for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But after soaring from S$1.3770 when the MAS policy statement was released to a new all-time high of S$1.3551 Thursday, the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  settled into a tight range Friday.\par \par \uc2 The intraday low for the greenback was S$1.3572, while the intraday high was S$1.3596.\par \par \uc2 "It's just profit taking after yesterday's (Thursday's) big move," a trader with a foreign bank said.\par \par \uc2 Another trader with a foreign bank said the market may be holding back from pushing the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar any higher to avoid a MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . With estimates on the top of the monetary policy band ranging from 1.3450 to 1.3560, the market may be acting cautiously to protect itself.\par \par \uc2 Still, traders said expectations of continued U.S. dollar weakness will likely fuel further appreciation. A local strategist also said the MAS' decision to tighten policy in two consecutive meetings is an indicator of the Singapore government's growing concern over inflationary pressures. The decision will likely translate into further strengthening of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The local government bond market fell slightly on low volume, tracking the U.S. Treasurys, a trader with a foreign bank said.\par \par \uc2 -By Se Young Lee, Dow Jones Newswires; 65 6415 4155; vincent.lee@dowjones.com [ 11-04-08 0716GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1163 1859   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020080411e44b000cd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
