\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: SGD Hits Record High After MAS Tightens Policy\b0\par\par\uc2 562 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 April 2008\par 03:33\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    (Adds market response, comments from economists.) \par  \par    By John Jannarone \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar rocketed to an all-time high Thursday after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  aggressively tightened policy to fight mounting inflationary pressures.\f28 \par \par \uc2 The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  went into temporary free-fall against the local dollar, dropping to a record low of S$1.3616 from S$1.3790 just before the policy statement release at 0000 GMT.\par \par \uc2 At 0130 GMT the greenback was at S$1.3627.\par \par \uc2 Analysts said the Singapore dollar may continue to rise under the new policy stance, and any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  would reflect an effort to slow, but not block further gains.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  made an implicit 1%-1.5% tightening," said Joseph Tan, senior strategist at Fortis Bank in Singapore.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore said it would re-center its undisclosed trade-weighted policy band for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which analysts believe to have a width of 2%-3%.\par \par \uc2 The MAS said in the statement that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has fluctuated near the top of the policy band since the last meeting in October.\par \par \uc2 "The U.S. dollar could fall to S$1.3560 after the tightening," said Selena Ling, an economist at Singapore's \uc2 OCBC Bank.\par \par \uc2 Similarly, \uc2 UBS\uc2  estimates that the U.S. dollar could fall to S$1.3500 without exceeding the limits of the new policy.\par \par \uc2 The policy tightening shows that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is making price stability a priority as the economy feels the impact of weaker global demand just as food and commodity prices surge.\par \par \uc2 But Ling said first quarter economic growth data, also issued Thursday, may have given the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  some comfort in its decision.\par \par \uc2 On a seasonally-adjusted annualized basis, gross domestic product grew 16.9% in the first quarter, reversing the 4.8% contraction in the previous quarter, according to the Ministry of Trade and Industry's advance estimate.\par \par \uc2 A Dow Jones Newswires Poll of economists had forecast a 6.8% rise.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  maintained its 4%-6% economic growth target for 2008, but warned that price pressures have intensified, likely leading 2008 inflation to come in at the top of its 4.5%-5.5% target range.\par \par \uc2 "CPI inflation has increased and is expected to remain elevated in the first half of this year," the MAS said.\par \par \uc2 "Against this backdrop of continuing external and domestic cost pressures, an upward shift of the policy band at this point will help to moderate inflation going forward, while providing support for sustainable growth in the economy."\par \par \uc2 The MAS uses exchange-rate targeting rather than interest rates as its chief policy tool because external trade dwarfs the domestic economy.\par \par \uc2 Thursday's policy shift follows a move at the last policy review in October to increase the slope of the trade-weighted band.\par \par \uc2 In recent months, consumer prices have risen at their fastest rate in 25 years as surging global food and energy costs have added to higher rents across the island.\par \par \uc2 The island's economy expanded 7.2% from a year earlier, faster than the 5.4% rise in the fourth quarter and higher than a poll forecast for a 5.7% growth.\par \par \uc2 -By John Jannarone, Dow Jones Newswires; 65 6415 4153; john.jannarone@dowjones.com [ 10-04-08 0133GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020080410e44a00039\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
