\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dlr Down Late Fri; Off All-Time High On MAS Selling   \b0\par\par\uc2 356 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2008\par 08:41\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                          Latest   Change \par    USD/SGD              1.3837   +0.0028 \par    Overnight rate        0.56%   +12 bps \par    Two-year bond yield:  0.89%   Unchanged \par    10-year bond yield:   2.07%   +3 bps \par    Two-year swap offer:  1.45%   -5 bps \par    10-year swap offer:   3.00%   -2 bps \par    2-10-yr swap curve:   155 bps +3 bps \par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar weakened late Friday in Asian spot trade after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore stepped in to take the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  off a fresh all-time high against the U.S. dollar.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 The U.S. unit hit a new low of S$1.3775 in early trade on expectations that the U.S. Federal Reserve will cut its benchmark interest rate by up to 75 basis points next week, due to heightened expectations that the world's largest economy may already be in recession.   \par \par \uc2 But traders said the MAS entered the market in force, buying over US$100 million to beat the Singapore dollar back from the top of its undisclosed policy band. The MAS uses the exchange rate as a policy tool.   \par \par \uc2 "They were definitely buying, starting at around S$1.3795," a local trader said.   \par \par \uc2 Traders told Dow Jones Newswires on Thursday that the MAS had sold at least S$5 billion since late last week to slow the local unit's appreciation. The Singapore government has said an overly strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would hurt the export-dependent economy.   \par \par \uc2 But a trader with a foreign bank said it is unlikely that today's events will cause the market to pause next week in driving up the Singapore dollar, as the greenback's slide is expected to continue on persisting concerns about the health of the U.S. economy.   \par \par \uc2 Local government bonds ended flat, a trader with a foreign bank said, as the tide of cash inflows seen in previous days ebbed after the MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar.   \par \par \uc2 -By Se Young Lee, Dow Jones Newswires; 65 6415 4155; vincent.lee@dowjones.com [ 14-03-08 0741GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 1163 1859   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020080314e43e000an\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
