\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Asia steadies, Taiwan and Singapore dollar up   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Melissa Chia   \par \uc2 736 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2008\par 04:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, March 4 (Reuters) - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose on Tuesday, some recovering from steep falls in previous sessions and others boosted by investors seeking yield after U.S. factory activity data reinforced expectations for further U.S. rate cuts.   \par \par \uc2 The U.S. data was better than expected, but showed the manufacturing sector was contracting. Meanwhile, euro zone officials said they shared Washington's preference for a strong dollar and were concerned about its excessive fall.   \par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar, Indonesian rupiah and Taiwan dollar climbed at least 0.3 percent each, while other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose but stayed in tight ranges as investors remained cautious and watched the steady dollar against the euro and major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 "Markets are looking for better levels to sell U.S. dollars in anticipation of Fed rates cut this month," said a trader in Jakarta, explaining the tight ranges of regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  speckled with sales of the U.S. dollar.   \par \par \uc2 The Taiwan dollar <TWD=TP> was an exception to the trend, rising by 0.8 percent to hit 30.8470, underpinned by fund inflows and firm equities as local stocks <.TWII> inched up by 2.5 percent to a 2-month high.[nTPF000691]   \par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar <SGD=> rose by 0.3 percent to hit 1.3905 per dollar as it continued its climb past the significant mark of 1.4 which it scaled last week.   \par \par \uc2 "Investment names continued to sell the U.S. dollar overnight, while the buy bid of 1.39 held well," a trader in Singapore said.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded in a tight range between 1.3925 and 1.3905, and analysts at Westpac Bank suspected the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was at the top of its secret policy band.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore (MAS), manages the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by allowing it to move against an undisclosed basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of its major trading partners, or the Nominal Effective Exchange Rate (NEER).   \par \par \uc2 "On our numbers, S$NEER is now high enough for dollar/\b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar to be firmly back in MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  territory,"  \uc2 Westpac\uc2  said in a note.   \par \par \uc2 Trading was cautious after European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Jean-Claude Trichet and other euro zone officials expressed concern over "excessive exchange rate moves" and indicated the dollar's slide to lifetime lows against the euro was undesirable.   \par \par \uc2 The Indonesian rupiah <IDR=> also rose by 0.3 percent to hit 9,085 per dollar, underpinned by the recovery in high yielders.   \par \par \uc2 "Overall, Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are still in favour so when there is a rally, people see it as an opportunity to sell the dollar," a trader in Jakarta said.   \par \par \uc2 Indonesia's inflation in February was in line with expectations at an annual rate of 7.4 percent and analysts expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep interest rates steady at 8 percent when it meets on Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 Other policy meetings investors are watching out for this week include the central banks of Japan, Korea, New Zealand, England and the euro zone.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  Change on the day at   0722 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       103.37         102.70       -0.65\par  Sing dlr        1.3907         1.3947       +0.29\par  Taiwan dlr      30.934         31.102       +0.54\par  Korean won      947.10         947.00       -0.01\par  Baht             31.61          31.62       +0.03\par  Peso             40.56          40.75       +0.47\par  Rupiah         9095.00        9118.00       +0.25\par  Rupee            40.30          40.38       +0.20\par  Ringgit         3.1900         3.1995       +0.30\par  Yuan            7.1073         7.1041       -0.05\par  Change so far in 2008\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       103.37         111.33       +7.70\par  Sing dlr        1.3907         1.4382       +3.42\par  Taiwan dlr      30.934         32.443       +4.88\par  Korean won      947.10         935.70       -1.20\par  Baht             31.61          33.68       +6.55\par  Peso             40.56          41.28       +1.78\par  Rupiah         9095.00        9390.00       +3.24\par  Rupee            40.30          39.41       -2.20\par  Ringgit         3.1900         3.3050       +3.61\par  Yuan            7.1073         7.3041       +2.77 (Reporting\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 by Melissa Chia; Editing by Tomasz Janowski)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ASIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|IF|PHD|SI|Z|J|SNS|SNI|RNP|DNP|PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080307e4340007p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
