\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Asian  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  rise, some hit decade highs   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Kevin Yao   \par \uc2 845 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Februar 2008\par 04:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Feb 27 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  firmed strongly on Wednesday, propelled by the prospects of falling U.S. interest rates, with some hitting their strongest levels since 1997.   \par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar <SGD=> rose as far as 1.3979 as the U.S. dollar slumped to a record low against the euro <EUR=> and a basket of major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  <.DXY>.   \par \par \uc2 It marked the first time that the Singapore dollar had pierced S$1.4 since January 1997, just before the Asia financial crisis.   \par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar was also supported by expectations the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  needs a stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb price pressures. Data on Monday showed the island's annual inflation accelerated to a 25-year high of 6.6 percent in January.   \par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar gained almost half of a percent on Wednesday, bringing its appreciation versus the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  so far this year to 2.9 percent.   \par \par \uc2 The Malaysian ringgit <MYR=> rose as far as 3.201 per dollar, up about 0.3 percent and its highest since late 1997. The Thai baht <THB=TH> briefly hit 32.09 per dollar, up half of a percent to its highest since August 1997.   \par \par \uc2 "The dollar/baht is still heavy from exporters' dollar sales plus expectations about lifting capital controls," said a trader in Bangkok.   \par \par \uc2 Investors believe Thai authorities will soon scrap capital controls imposed in late 2006, which were designed to curb the baht's strength to protect local exporters.   \par \par \uc2 The Bank of Thailand kept its policy interest rate steady at 3.25 percent on Wednesday, as expected.   \par \par \uc2 The Thai rate -- the lowest in emerging Asia, is still higher than the U.S. fed funds rate, which has fallen rapidly to 3 percent.   \par \par \uc2 The Indonesian rupiah <IDR=> hit 9,037 per dollar, up almost 0.6 percent from late Asian trade on Tuesday.   \par \par \uc2 "Unless there is another wave of inflows today, the rupiah should retrace a bit," said a trader in Jakarta.   \par \par \uc2 WEAK DOLLAR AND INFLATION   \par \par \uc2 The dollar slumped after weak economic data and comments from a Fed official signalled that U.S. interest rates will continue to head lower. [ID:nN26322234]   \par \par \uc2 Fed Vice Chairman Donald Kohn said on Tuesday that a weak U.S. economy was a bigger worry than higher inflation risks. [ID:nN26364877]   \par \par \uc2 Fed Chairman Ben Bernanke is expected to provide a similar message when he presents the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's twice-yearly monetary policy report to Congress on Wednesday and Thursday. [ID:nN24651396]   \par \par \uc2 In Asia, inflation risks are likely to prod policy makers to tolerate stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb import costs, fuelled by lofty oil prices, analysts said.   \par \par \uc2 "The driver for Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a combination of a Fed being backed into further cuts amid a climate of rising global inflation," said Claudio Piron, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at  \uc2 JPMorgan.\par \par \uc2 "Singapore is uniquely positioned in that its \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate is the tool of choice in combating inflation and is widely seen as credibly applied," he added.   \par \par \uc2 But he cautioned that \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would keep \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to ensure \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rises are gradual.   \par \par \uc2 The Taiwan dollar <TWD=TP> hit a three-year high at 30.903 per U.S. dollar amid fund inflows, bringing its gains this year to 5 percent, overtaking the baht as Asia's top performer.   \par \par \uc2 The Chinese yuan <CNY=CFXS> rose to 7.1450 per dollar but was still off its post-revaluation high at 7.1413 hit last week.   \par \par \uc2 Many analysts expect China to let the yuan rise around 10 percent this year, compared to 6.9 percent in 2007, to fight inflation, which hit a 11-year high of 7.1 percent in January. \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on the day at 0821 GMT    \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       106.89         108.03       +1.07\par  Sing dlr        1.3977         1.4043       +0.47\par  Taiwan dlr      30.903         31.210       +0.99\par  Korean won      940.80         947.10       +0.67\par  Baht             32.12          32.26       +0.44\par  Peso             40.22          40.47       +0.62\par  Rupiah         9050.00        9089.00       +0.43\par  Rupee            39.71          39.90       +0.47\par  Ringgit         3.2015         3.2120       +0.33\par  Yuan            7.1473         7.1580       +0.15\par  Change so far in 2008\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       106.89         111.33       +4.15\par  Sing dlr        1.3977         1.4382       +2.90\par  Taiwan dlr      30.903         32.443       +4.98\par  Korean won      940.80         935.70       -0.54\par  Baht             32.12          33.68       +4.86\par  Peso             40.22          41.28       +2.64\par  Rupiah         9050.00        9390.00      