\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  dollar capped by c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 -traders   \b0\par\par\uc2 255 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Februar 2008\par 07:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Feb 25 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was suspected of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Monday as the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar rose to an 11-year-high of S$1.4050 and as data showed inflation at its highest since 1982, traders said.   \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar <SGD=> eased back to S$1.4060 per U.S. dollar from the high as dealers suspected the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was buying U.S. dollars.   \par \par \uc2  "The granny (\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) is around," said a Singapore-based trader. "They have been there since last week, but all they can do is slow the pace of the U.S. dollar's decline."   \par \par \uc2  A second dealer agreed: "I reckon they will try to prevent spot falling below S$1.4050."   \par \par \uc2  Still, dealers and analysts said they expected the Singapore dollar to rise beyond the S$1.4 level in the near term as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is under pressure to quell inflation even as economic growth slows.   \par \par \uc2  Analysts also estimate the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is at the top end of its undisclosed policy band, based on the value of a trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , within which the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore (MAS) manages the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2  Consumer prices in January rose 6.6 percent from a year earlier, the fastest pace since 1982, government data showed on Monday. [ID:nSGC001786] [SGCPIY=ECI]  (Reporting by Kevin Yao; Editing by Neil Fullick)     \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-SINGAPORE/DOLLAR|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|SI|ABX|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080225e42p000cp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
