\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dollar Ends Tad Higher;MAS Fears Suppress Gains   \b0\par\par\uc2 322 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Februar 2008\par 08:16\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                          Latest   Change \par    USD/SGD               1.4155   -0.0010 \par    Overnight rate        1.75%    -6 bps \par    Two-year bond yield:  1.38%    Unchanged \par    10-year bond yield:   2.21%    Unchanged \par    Two-year swap offer:  1.80%    -3 bps \par    10-year swap offer:   2.95%    -6 bp \par    2-10-yr swap curve:   115 bps  -3 bps \par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)-- The Singapore dollar rose slightly on continued weakness in the U.S. Dollar in Asian trade Friday, but gains were limited as investors tread carefully to avoid provoking the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  into \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to slow the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's appreciation.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Traders said the greenback continued to slide against the Singapore dollar and other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  due to the slowdown in the U.S. economy and the sharp recent interest rate cuts by the U.S. Federal Reserve.   \par \par \uc2 However, the downward momentum has been balanced by caution due to the possibility that the MAS could step into the market if the Singapore dollar starts to move too quickly, traders said.   \par \par \uc2 "Overnight there were rumors of an official presence, so the market is a little bit cautious today," said a local trader.   \par \par \uc2 The trader said the U.S. dollar's current trading levels are near the strong end of the MAS policy band, indicating that there is reason to be wary.   \par \par \uc2 While the downward bias for the U.S. dollar is expected to continue, traders said the December U.S. non-farm payrolls report due later Friday could also move the market next week.   \par \par \uc2 Government bond trading was also quiet in low volumes, with no major news to push the market ahead of the payrolls data. A local trader said some of the primary dealers weren't around for today's session, contributing to the inactivity.   \par \par \uc2 -By Se Young Lee, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4155; vincent.lee@dowjones.com [ 01-02-08 0716GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 1163 1859   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020080201e421000cx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
