\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dollar Flat On MAS Concerns, Weak Asian Equities   \b0\par\par\uc2 336 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Januar 2008\par 08:35\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                          Latest   Change \par    USD/SGD               1.4294   -0.0005 \par    Overnight rate        1.25%    +6 bps \par    Two-year bond yield:  1.48%    -3 bps \par    10-year bond yield:   2.29%    -3 bps \par    Two-year swap offer:  2.04%    -6 bps \par    10-year swap offer:   3.06%    -1 bp \par    2-10-yr swap curve:   102 bps  +5 bps    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar was little changed in Asian trade Monday, with the market cautious due to concerns of further \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the U.S. dollar continued its fall against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as the U.S. Federal Reserve is expected to cut interest rates by 50 basis points when it meets later in January.   \par \par \uc2 But traders said prospects of further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the MAS are holding them back. On Friday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in to slow the appreciation of the Singapore dollar after the greenback fell to a 10-year-low of S$1.4257.   \par \par \uc2 "Like other central banks in the region, they do step in to slow down the volatility," a local trader said.   \par \par \uc2 Weakness among Asian bourses along with Wall Street's selloff Friday has also diminished investors' risk appetite, another local trader said. This has damped demand for the Singapore dollar, leaving the pair to tread water in Monday's session.   \par \par \uc2 But traders said the greenback's fall will likely continue, as a series of economic data to be released in the U.S. this week could expose further weakness in the economy.   \par \par \uc2 Local bonds continued to rise after big gains Friday. Continued buying interest on the short-term papers led to a further steepening of the yield curve.   \par \par \uc2 "On the back of U.S. Treasurys, Singapore government papers continue on a price increase," a local trader said, noting that investors were fleeing the languishing equities markets.   \par \par \uc2 -By Se Young Lee, Dow Jones Newswires; 65 6415 4155; vincent.lee@dowjones.com [ 14-01-08 0735GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 1163 1859   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020080114e41e000ay\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
