\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Asia listless amid uncertainty,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 806 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Januar 2008\par 04:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Jan 10 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were steady on Thursday as investors held back because of uncertainty over the outlook for the U.S. economy and rate decisions due in Europe later in the day.   \par \par \uc2  Traders said the market was also cautious because central banks in the Philippines, Malaysia, India and \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  were suspected of having \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week to curb strength in their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar recovered against the yen and other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  overnight and held near a nine-month high against sterling <GBP=> in Asia.   \par \par \uc2  But Asian stock markets <0#.INDEXA>, where foreigners have been heavy net sellers this year, barely moved, giving little direction to \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2  The South Korean won <KRW=> initially rose 0.3 percent to hit 934.0 per dollar as local equities <.KS11> rallied, but it soon pared the gains to trade around 937.   \par \par \uc2  A trader in Seoul said the won was stuck between 933 and 945 per dollar.   \par \par \uc2  "There's a solid bottom for the dollar at 930 because oil companies are buying more dollars and equity outflows are continuing," the trader said.   \par \par \uc2  "But there's also interest from shipping companies to hedge their earnings above 940 and exporters are selling options," she said.   \par \par \uc2  Another trader felt the won would weaken to around 970 per dollar over the next few weeks, owing to outflows for dividend payments and  \uc2 SK Telecom\uc2 's purchase of a stake in Korean broadband provider  \uc2 hanarotelecom\uc2  , valued at nearly $1.2 billion.   \par \par \uc2  SK is buying the stake from a consortium led by  \uc2 American International Group\uc2  and private equity fund Newbridge Capital.   \par \par \uc2  Options traders said there was demand to sell won around 940 for one month and up to 1,000 per dollar through one-year options.   \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the Singapore dollar <SGD=> was steady around 1.4310 per U.S. dollar while the Philippine peso <PHP=> fell half a percent from its previous close, backing off the highest level in nearly eight years hit on Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2  In a volatile session, the peso rose from a low of 40.78 per dollar to hover around 40.60 before slipping again in late trading as the dollar gained against sterling and the yen.   \par \par \uc2  "I think the peso will still appreciate. Any dollar upticks will be sold," a trader in Manila said.   \par \par \uc2  But some analysts said the peso's long rally may have run its course for now.   \par \par \uc2  They said a report earlier on Thursday showing Philippine exports in November fell 2 percent from a year earlier raised worries the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 20 percent appreciation in the past 12 months may be hurting the economy.   \par \par \uc2  Many investors kept to the sidelines ahead of meetings by the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB) and Bank of England (BoE), and a speech by Federal Reserve Chairman Ben Bernanke later on Thursday.   \par \par \uc2  Analysts expect the ECB to hold interest rates steady at 4.0 percent but see the BoE cutting rates due to weak consumption, which has sparked fears of a slowdown in the economy.   \par \par \uc2  The next Fed rates decision is due on Jan. 30 and market expectations are shifting increasingly towards a cut in the Fed funds rate of as much as 50 basis points, although the majority in a Reuters poll still expected a more modest 25 basis points.    \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  Change on the day at   0757 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       109.81         109.48       -0.30\par  Sing dlr        1.4315         1.4306       -0.06\par  Taiwan dlr      32.489         32.466       -0.07\par  Korean won      937.40         937.20       -0.02\par  Baht             33.14          33.15       +0.03\par  Peso             40.75          40.56       -0.47\par  Rupiah         9430.00        9448.00       +0.19\par  Rupee            39.29          39.28       -0.01\par  Ringgit         3.2673         3.2650       -0.07\par  Yuan            7.2695         7.2620       -0.10\par  Change so far in 2008\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       109.81         111.33       +1.38\par  Sing dlr        1.4315         1.4382       +0.47\par  Taiwan dlr      32.489         32.443       -0.14\par  Korean won      937.40         935.70       -0.18\par  Baht             33.14          33.68       +1.63\par  Peso             40.75          41.28       +1.30\par  Rupiah         9430.00        9390.00       -0.42\par  Rupee            39.29          39.41       +0.32\par  Ringgit         3.2673         3.3050       +1.15\par  Yuan            7.2695         7.3041       +0.48\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  (Reporting by Melissa Chia and Vidya Ranganathan; Editing by\par Alan Raybould) ((melissa.chia@reuters.com;+65-68703840; Reuters\par Messaging: melissa.chia.reuters.com@reuters.net))   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  For the new Reuters scrolling global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  service please\par click <FXNEWS>\par \par \