\par\par \b \uc2 Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dollar Nudges Higher As Market Reverses ISM Sales   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Karen Lane   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 597 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Januar 2008\par 06:31\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The U.S. dollar pulled gently higher against the yen Thursday as players started to reverse early sales and take off some positions that have sent the U.S. unit some Y5 lower since Dec. 27.   \par \par \uc2 The euro also came off its highs against its U.S. counterpart.   \par \par \uc2 But traders remain nervous about the dollar in the wake of a discouraging manufacturing survey overnight and in the run-up to key jobs data due to be released Friday.   \par \par \uc2 The Institute of Supply Management's December manufacturing index, which contracted after 10 consecutive months of expansion, prompted a drop in U.S. stocks and a spike in risk aversion. In turn, the trading day started on a sour note for the dollar before some light buying kicked in.   \par \par \uc2 U.S. jobs data out Friday should provide more clues to the direction of the economy, traders said.   \par \par \uc2 But "very weak" jobs data will be needed for the yen, euro, sterling and Australian dollar to break above key resistance levels against the dollar, said Easy \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  senior dealer Francisco Solar, noting the U.S. labor market has been resilient and largely supportive of the economy so far.   \par \par \uc2 He pegged resistance for the euro at $1.48, at $0.8850 for the Australian dollar and at $2.00 for sterling.   \par \par \uc2 Another Singapore-based trader said strong buy orders for the dollar are placed at Y109.20-Y109.25 and Y108.70 and Y108.75.   \par \par \uc2 Economists forecast that U.S. non farm payrolls will rise an average 50,000 in December after a 94,000 rise in November.   \par \par \uc2 The dollar hit a high of around Y114.65 on Dec. 27 but was at Y109.68 at 0518 GMT, off its intraday low of around Y109.24. The euro was at $1.4710, off its high hit earlier in the morning of around $1.4725.   \par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, the U.S. dollar sank to S$1.4350, its lowest against the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since July 1997. By early afternoon, though, it had nudged off that low as players turned wary about \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  now very close of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy band.   \par \par \uc2 The U.S. unit was at S$1.4361, down from the S$1.4386 close Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                         Latest     Previous   %Chg   Daily   Daily    %Chg \par Dollar Rates                        2150 GMT          High    Low      12/31 \par USD/JPY Yen              109.66-69  109.54-60  +0.11  109.75  109.24   -7.90 \par EUR/USD Euro             1.4711-14  1.4724-27  -0.09  1.4725  1.4698  +11.46 \par GBP/USD Sterling         1.9830-33  1.9815-18  +0.08  1.9839  1.9799   +1.18 \par USD/CHF Swiss Franc      1.1183-87  1.1184-89  -0.01  1.12    1.1179   -8.20 \par USD/CAD Canadian Dlr     0.9945-48  0.9931-37  +0.14  0.9954  0.9922  -14.68 \par AUD/USD Australian Dlr   0.8832-37  0.8835-40  -0.03  0.8850  0.8816  +11.90 \par NZD/USD New Zealand Dlr  0.7746-52  0.7753-59  -0.09  0.7760  0.7734   +9.95 \par  \par Euro Rates \par EUR/JPY Yen              161.33-38  161.35-38  -0.01  161.62  160.80   +2.65 \par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Karen Lane, Dow Jones Newswires; 65 6415 4043; karen.lane@dowjones.com   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Jerry Tan in Singapore and Sam Holmes in Sydney contributed to this report.) [ 03-01-08 0531GMT ]   \f28 \par \par \uc2 1034 1863 28038 4162   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020080103e4130003d\