\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dollar Ends Flat; Held Back By Fear Of  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 336 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Dezember 2007\par 09:19\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                          Latest   Change \par    USD/SGD               1.4422   +0.0003 \par    Overnight rate        1.19%    +19bps \par    Two-year bond yield:  1.82%    -8 bps \par    10-year bond yield:   2.81%    -3 bps \par    Two-year swap offer:  2.78%    -4 bps \par    10-year swap offer:   3.48%    -4bps \par    2-10-yr swap curve:   70 bpsUnchanged \par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)-- The Singapore dollar finished flat in Asian trade Wednesday despite a selloff on Wall Street, as traders remained cautious after suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  the previous day.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, the U.S. Federal Reserve cut interest rates by 25 basis points to 4.25%. Wall Street, however, did not think the cut was big enough, resulting in a 2.1% drop in the Dow Jones Industrial Average to 13,432.77 points.   \par \par \uc2 A local trader said support for the U.S. dollar should hold around S$1.44 for the near term, as the rate cut was already priced in and investors weren't anxious to challenge the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 "All the few dips we've seen below 1.44 have failed," the trader said. "People are just a little bit cautious on the downside."   \par \par \uc2 The trader said there were concerns about the possibility of further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which was suspected to have entered the market Tuesday when the greenback hit a low of S$1.4372.   \par \par \uc2 But traders said the Singapore dollar is likely to continue to appreciate over time along with other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . One local trader said the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has no choice but to allow the appreciation due to inflation.   \par \par \uc2 Local government bond prices rose in late trade on buying by foreign investors, especially in short-to-medium terms, to park the Singapore dollars they have been buying in anticipation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's further appreciation.   \par \par \uc2 -By Se Young Lee, Dow Jones Newswires; 65 6415 4154; vincent.lee@dowjones.com [ 12-12-07 0819GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 1163 1859   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020071212e3cc000bq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
