\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  Dollar Ends Tad Lower, Some Suspect  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 342 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Dezember 2007\par 08:30\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                          Latest   Change \par    USD/SGD               1.4419   +0.0010 \par    Overnight rate        1.00%    -6 bps \par    Two-year bond yield:  1.90%    Unchanged \par    10-year bond yield:   2.84%    +1 bps \par    Two-year swap offer:  2.82%    +1 bps \par    10-year swap offer:   3.52%    +2 bps \par    2-10-yr swap curve:   70 bps   +1 bps \par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar finished marginally lower in Asian trade Tuesday as traders saw some large buying interest in the U.S. dollar.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Some traders suspect that Singapore's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could have been in the market, buying the greenback after it hit an intra-day low of S$1.4372, close to a 10-year low of S$1.4363 tested in November.   \par \par \uc2 "There was a sudden spike in the U.S. dollar from S$1.4382, and there was (follow-through) buying interest," said a trader.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore, which has said that it prefers a modest and gradual appreciation of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against its major trading \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , doesn't comment on its market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 Traders now await the outcome of December's Federal Open Market Committee in the U.S. later tonight.   \par \par \uc2 Though most expect the Fed to cut interest rate by 25 basis points, a 50-basis point cut could send the US dollar sliding against higher-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as risk appetite will increase further.   \par \par \uc2 "The reaction of Wall Street to the Fed meeting will be a key driver for Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said another trader.   \par \par \uc2 Local government bond yields were flat on thin volumes as players were sitting on the sidelines ahead of the Fed meeting.   \par \par \uc2 "Given concerns of domestic inflation and with the market the already having discounted a 25 basis points interest rate cut by Fed, there isn't much movement that could be seen in the bond market," said a trader.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    -By P.R. Venkat, Dow Jones Newswires; +65 64154 152, venkat.pr@dowjones.com \par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 11-12-07 0730GMT ]   \f28 \par \par \uc2 1163 1859   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020071211e3cb000af\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
