ll Street to the Fed meeting will be a key driver for Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said another trader. Local government bond yields were flat on thin volumes as players were sitting on the sidelines ahead of the Fed meeting. "Given concerns of domestic inflation and with the market the already having discounted a 25 basis points interest rate cut by Fed, there isn't much movement that could be seen in the bond market," said a trader. -By P.R. Venkat, Dow Jones Newswires; +65 64154 152, venkat.pr@dowjones.com -0-    \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020071211e3cb002pa\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
