\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dollar Ends Higher, Awaits US Econ Data; Bonds Rise   \b0\par\par\uc2 338 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Dezember 2007\par 08:28\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                          Latest   Change \par    USD/SGD               1.4484   -0.0040 \par    Overnight rate        0.81%    -12 bps \par    Two-year bond yield:  1.87%    -11 bps \par    10-year bond yield:   2.73%    -6 bps \par    Two-year swap offer:  2.73%    -2 bps \par    10-year swap offer:   3.38%    -2 bps \par    2-10-yr swap curve:   65 bps   Unchanged \par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar ended higher in Asian trade Tuesday as investors were selling U.S. dollars, given the greenback's weak outlook, while the absence of an \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the past few sessions boosted the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , traders said.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 They, however, said that investors were still cautious about placing any big bets, as they await the U.S. non-farm payrolls data due Friday that might give hint to the Federal Reserve's decision on policy rates at its Federal Open Market Committee meeting next week.   \par \par \uc2 The fact that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't been in the market since its last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday gave comfort to some investors selling U.S. dollars, said a trader with a foreign bank.   \par \par \uc2 The MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on that day to stem a rise in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 "The U.S. dollar is likely to remain slightly heavy till the outcome of the FOMC meeting next week," said another trader with a local bank.   \par \par \uc2 In the local bond market, prices rose as they were tracking the overnight gains in U.S. Treasurys.   \par \par \uc2 "There has been a demand for the two-year and 10-year papers," said a trader with a foreign bank.   \par \par \uc2 Also, he said that the liquidity in the market remained flush as the MAS withdrew S$1.4 billion from the market Tuesday.   \par \par \uc2 On Monday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  withdrew S$1.9 billion from the market - as part of its money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  - to avoid excess liquidity.   \par \par \uc2 -By P.R. Venkat, Dow Jones Newswires; 65 64154 152, venkat.pr@dowjones.com [ 04-12-07 0728GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 1163 1859   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020071204e3c40008z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
