prices rose as they were tracking the overnight gains in U.S. Treasurys. 'There has been a demand for the two-year and 10-year papers,' said a trader with a foreign bank. Also, he said that the liquidity in the market remained flush as the MAS withdrew S$1.4 billion from the market Tuesday. On Monday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  withdrew S$1.9 billion from the market - as part of its money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  - to avoid excess liquidity. -By P.R. Venkat, Dow Jones Newswires; 65 64154 152, venkat.pr@dowjones.com -0-    \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020071204e3c4003bh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
