\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  Dollar Gains Despite Apparent MAS  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 370 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Oktober 2007\par 11:39\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                          Latest   Change \par    USD/SGD               1.4553   -0.0030 \par    Overnight rate        2.06%    +31 bps \par    Two-year bond yield:  1.92%    +7 bps \par    10-year bond yield:   2.75%    +2 bps \par    Two-year swap offer:  2.73%    +2 bps \par    10-year swap offer:   3.23%    +3 bps \par    2-10-yr swap curve:   50 bps   +1 bp \par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar finished the week on a strong note Friday even as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  apparently \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to interrupt a broad-based decline in the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Traders said the Singapore dollar may be locked in a range next week as foreign inflows are offset by speculation that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore will act again to protect the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  band.   \par \par \uc2 Two traders told Dow Jones Newswires the MAS bought U.S. dollars as the greenback dropped to a 10-year low at S$1.4523. They didn't specify the size of the transaction, but the MAS has accumulated billions of U.S. dollars on a single day when making purchases in the past.   \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was (buying U.S. dollars) from around S$1.4523 and the market whipped up (the greenback) to S$1.4592," one of the traders said.   \par \par \uc2 The MAS manages the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within a secret trade-weighted band and currently allows a modest, gradual appreciation of the Singapore dollar.   \par \par \uc2 Analytical models at many investment banks indicated the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was near or above the upper limit of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  band earlier Friday.   \par \par \uc2 At S$1.4523, the U.S. dollar was at its lowest since June 1997.   \par \par \uc2 In the government bond market, prices fell as traders booked gains from a string of rallies earlier in the week.   \par \par \uc2 "There was a feeling that it was time to take some profit, but prices should be supported as the foreign inflows are still coming," a trader said.   \par \par \uc2 The yield on the benchmark 2-year Singapore government bond dropped to an intraday low of 1.82% earlier in the week, the lowest since February 2005.   \par \par \uc2 -By John Jannarone, Dow Jones Newswires; 65 6415 4153; john.jannarone@dowjones.com [ 26-10-07 0939GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 1163 1859   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020071026e3aq000ss\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
