\par\par \b \uc2 MAS Tightening Puts Singapore Dollar On Track For New Record   \b0\par\par\uc2 By John Jannarone   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 800 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Oktober 2007\par 12:53\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--A surprise monetary tightening by Singapore's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday vaulted the Singapore dollar up sharply and put it on track to rise to its all-time high set during the 1990s boom.   \par \par \uc2 The stronger Singapore dollar will help cap mounting price pressures in the city state but won't cause exporters to lose their competitive footing against regional rivals because other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are also on an upward course against a swooning U.S. dollar, analysts say.   \par \par \uc2 "The stronger Singapore dollar is not going to put a massive downward pressure on exports," said Prakriti Sofat, an economist at  \uc2 HSBC\uc2  in Singapore.   \par \par \uc2 "The appreciation is still going to be very gradual and we think the government is going to be very cautious about maintaining economic growth."   \par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar sprung to a 10-year high against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  early Wednesday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore said it would "increase slightly" the slope of its undisclosed trade-weighted \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  band. The U.S. dollar fell to S$1.4631 - a point last reached in July 1997 - from S$1.4720 just before the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  issued the statement.   \par \par \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  economist Chua Hak Bin said the new policy may allow the trade-weighted \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rise an extra 0.2-0.5 percentage point each year beyond the estimated 1.9% rate allowed previously. He now expects U.S. dollar to finish 2008 at S$1.3900 compared to a previous forecast of S$1.4100.   \par \par \uc2 That target is just above the Singapore dollar's record high set in May 1995, when the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fetched only S$1.3835. And the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  may approach the record more quickly if Singapore's red-hot economy maintains momentum, Chua said.   \par \par \uc2 "Further MAS tightening may be necessary next year, via more 'slight' fine-tuning," Chua said. "Lower Singapore dollar interest rates, following the Fed rate cuts, have moreover exacerbated demand pressures."   \par \par \uc2 The more hawkish stance by Singapore's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stems from concerns that rising inflation could pose a growing risk to the economy, which has been booming on growth in financial services and surging output of pharmaceuticals and offshore oil rigs.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's statement noted the local three-month interbank interest rate has fallen to about 2.5% from 3.5% in February. It forecast inflation will stay within a 1.5%-2% range this year and 2%-3% in 2008, but warned about the impending impact of rising residential rents and property prices.   \par \par \uc2 That means Singapore, which uses the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate to influence prices because external trade dwarfs the domestic economy, is likely willing to let its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rise at a moderately faster pace.   \par \par \uc2 "Against a robust growth backdrop, the MAS is clearly taking no chances when it comes to the inflation outlook, hence the tightening step,"  \uc2 Rabobank\uc2  said in a note to clients.   \par \par \uc2 Rabobank\uc2  now forecasts the U.S. dollar will drop to S$1.4300 by the end of 2008, lower than its forecast of S$1.4400 before the MAS policy statement.   \par \par \uc2 To be sure, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be vigilant against sharp swings in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates. It has demonstrated a willingness to keep a tight grip on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 JPMorgan Chase Bank and Societe Generale noted unconfirmed talk in the market Wednesday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cushion the U.S. dollar's early plunge, though other traders played down such speculation.   \par \par \uc2 Still, traders have said the MAS was active in the market during periods of heightened volatility last month to prevent drastic appreciation. And late last year the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  added tens of billions of U.S. dollars in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  forward exposure in an apparent effort stem the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise.   \par \par \uc2 HSBC\uc2 's Sofat said the strength in the Singapore dollar is in line with gains in other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The Singapore dollar has gained about 5% against the U.S. dollar in 2007 while the Chinese yuan has risen 4% and the Malaysian Ringgit is up nearly 10%.   \par \par \uc2 "The Singapore dollar has been appreciating, but the rest of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  across Asia are also moving higher," Sofat said. "The MAS is keeping a conservative view and it's unlikely we'll see exports threatened," she added.   \par \par \uc2 She said Singapore's economy may decelerate only slightly next year from the MAS's 7%-8% target for 2007.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it expects the economy to expand by 4%-6% in 2008, but both  \uc2 HSBC\uc2  and  \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  expect a higher rate of expansion.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    -By John Jannarone, Dow Jones Newswires; 65 6415 4153; john.jannarone@dowjones.com \par    -Edited by Arran Scott \par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 10-10-07 1053GMT ]   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020071010e3aa000l8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
