\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Singapore dollar at 10-yr high, rupiah rises   \b0\par\par\uc2 867 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Oktober 2007\par 05:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Oct 1 (Reuters) - The Singapore dollar <SGD=> hit a 10-year high on Monday, leading a rally in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  after weakness in U.S. inflation data renewed selling pressure in the U.S. dollar.   \par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar rose nearly 1 percent to hit 1.4765 per dollar, its strongest since July 1997.   \par \par \uc2 The Indonesian rupiah <IDR=> and Malaysian ringgit <MYR=> also gained strongly, each rising by at least half a percent.   \par \par \uc2 The rupiah hit a 2-month high of 9,079 per dollar. The Philippine peso <PHP=> hit a 2-month high of 44.85 per dollar, then stalled on fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The dollar hit another record low against both the euro <EUR=> and a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  after a tame reading in the Federal Reserve's favoured price index stoked expectations of another cut in U.S. rates.   \par \par \uc2 The dollar's decline was spurred by the Fed's large half point rate cut on Sept. 18, one that was designed to buffer the economy from the problems in the subprime mortgage sector.   \par \par \uc2 Traders expect trading volumes in Asia to thin this week as Chinese markets are closed for National Day holidays.   \par \par \uc2 Some also were getting nervous about selling the dollar too aggressively ahead of the Group of Seven nations' meeting in Washington in mid-October.   \par \par \uc2 "There is a sizeable short-dollar position," said  \uc2 Bank of America\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Han Sia Yeo.   \par \par \uc2 "The dollar could see a bounce this week on prospects of stronger-than-expected U.S. data," he said.   \par \par \uc2 OCBC Bank\uc2  strategist Emmanuel Ng said in a note he expected the momentum of dollar-selling to persist although there were signs of positions getting excessively extended.   \par \par \uc2 He also warned that Asian central banks could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow gains in the regionals.   \par \par \uc2 Analysts at DBS told investors to anticipate more volatility ahead of the G7 meeting.   \par \par \uc2 European policy makers have been calling for a stronger dollar and expressing worry about the euro's rapid rise.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Federal Reserve Governor Frederic Mishkin said last week Europe's economy will have to adapt with the changing value of the dollar.   \par \par \uc2 "The market will be looking out for rhetoric out of G7 officials that will suggest whether or not the U.S. dollar and the Chinese yuan will be mentioned in the G7 communique, something that the Europeans appear to favour, and the Americans opposed," DBS said in a note.   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE DOLLAR   \par \par \uc2 Traders, meanwhile, were pricing in more appreciation for the Singapore dollar, partly on belief the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore (MAS) will retain a gradual tightening bias when it reviews policy on Oct. 10.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is the MAS's main policy tool. It has gained more than 3 percent in the past three weeks, but traders estimated it was still on the weaker side of the secret trade-weighted or nominal-effective-exchange-rate (NEER) band within which the MAS guides the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 "Most of the people have missed out on this move as they kept thinking MAS would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at some point of time," a \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 -based trader said.   \par \par \uc2 "Technically, there aren't any supports for U.S. dollar before the 1.45-handle, so I think we have enough room to move to the downside, particularly in the run up to the monetary policy."   \par \par \uc2 Analysts at  \uc2 UBS\uc2  said the Singapore dollar had stayed within 0.65 percent of the mid-point of the MAS's policy band in the past four months. But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent upward revision to its inflation forecasts for the year suggested it was happy to have the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciate, they said.   \par \par \uc2 "This in our view signals the MAS is not about to let down its guard on inflation despite the recent market volatility. We think the MAS is pretty happy seeing the NEER rising,"  \uc2 UBS\uc2  said in a note. \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on the day at 0757 GMT    \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       115.57         115.33       -0.21\par  Sing dlr        1.4773         1.4903       +0.88\par  Taiwan dlr      32.558         32.580       +0.07\par  Korean won      913.60         915.00       +0.15\par  Baht             34.24          34.25       +0.03\par  Peso             44.85          45.04       +0.43\par  Rupiah         9082.00        9147.00       +0.72\par  Rupee            39.75          39.73       -0.05\par  Ringgit         3.3915         3.4115       +0.59\par  Change so far in 2007\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       115.57         119.01       +2.98\par  Sing dlr        1.4773         1.5337       +3.82\par  Taiwan dlr      32.558         32.585       +0.08\par  Korean won      913.60         929.50       +1.74\par  Baht             34.24          36.08       +5.37\par  Peso             44.85          49.03       +9.33\par  Rupiah    