\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 - \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  caps peso, but Taiwan dollar jumps   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Kevin Yao   \par \uc2 754 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 September 2007\par 05:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Sept 28 (Reuters) - The Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's suspected dollar buying stalled rises in the high-yielding peso on Friday, while the Taiwan dollar and South Korean won jumped as investors raised their bet on further U.S. interest rate cuts.   \par \par \uc2 The low-yielding Taiwan dollar <TWD=TP> rose as far as 32.50 per U.S. dollar, up 0.6 percent from Thursday's close to a nine-month high, amid signs that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was selling the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  along with local exporters.   \par \par \uc2 "They (the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) think the Taiwan dollar should strengthen slightly to help reduce the inflationary risk," said a trader in Singapore. "And the U.S. dollar/Asia go lower."   \par \par \uc2 The won <KRW=> gained 0.6 percent to 914.80 per dollar, a two-month high.   \par \par \uc2 The peso <PHP=> pulled back to the weaker side of 45 per dollar after its attempt to break the two-month peak of 44.90 was foiled by suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was spotted at the 44.90 level. There was also some mild profit-taking," said a trader in Manila.   \par \par \uc2 "Probably it wants to prevent a sharp drop for the dollar/peso to limit volatility," said a second trader.   \par \par \uc2 The peso has gained nearly 9 percent against the dollar so far this year, trailing behind the 11 percent gains in the Indian rupee <INR=IN>, another high-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asia.   \par \par \uc2 Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , led by the high-yielders, have rallied alongside rising regional stocks after the Federal Reserve cut its key interest rate by 50 basis points last Tuesday.   \par \par \uc2 "In general, we expect the trend to continue, maybe not at the (current) pace," said Magnus Prim, SEB's chief Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist.   \par \par \uc2 "We are positive on the rupiah and peso -- these two probably have more to go. The Singapore dollar is also one," he said.   \par \par \uc2 EYE ON U.S. ECONOMY   \par \par \uc2 The dollar stuck near record lows against the euro <EUR=> and a basket of major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  after U.S. data showed sales of new homes plunged in August, cementing expectations that the Fed would cut interest rates again next month.   \par \par \uc2 Investors awaited reports on U.S. business activity and inflation data to gauge the health of the world's largest economy and how far the Fed is likely to loosen its monetary policy further.   \par \par \uc2 The Indonesian rupiah <IDR=>, another high-yielder, moved in a tight range between 9,125 and 9,158 per dollar.   \par \par \uc2 "The rupiah might move between the 9,120 and 9,170 range for the next week," said a trader in Jakarta.   \par \par \uc2 Analysts are increasingly bullish about the rupiah, which remains the worst performer in Asia this year, but some caution that foreigners might pull out from the country's bond markets as higher inflation could stifle the chance of another rate cut.   \par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar <SGD=> hit a fresh 10-year high at 1.4887 to the U.S. dollar, bringing its gains in the past week to 1 percent amid expectations that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will stick to its modest tightening policy in a meeting early next month. \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on the day at 0807 GMT    \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       115.33         115.61       +0.24\par  Sing dlr        1.4903         1.4920       +0.11\par  Taiwan dlr      32.666         32.825       +0.49\par  Korean won      915.00         920.00       +0.55\par  Baht             34.25          34.26       +0.03\par  Peso             44.99          45.01       +0.04\par  Rupiah         9147.00        9140.00       -0.08\par  Rupee            39.75          39.70       -0.13\par  Ringgit         3.4115         3.4160       +0.13\par  Yuan            7.5112         7.5148       +0.05\par  Change so far in 2007\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       115.33         119.01       +3.19\par  Sing dlr        1.4903         1.5337       +2.91\par  Taiwan dlr      32.666         32.585       -0.25\par  Korean won      915.00         929.50       +1.58\par  Baht             34.25          36.08       +5.34\par  Peso             44.99          49.03       +8.98\par  Rupiah         9147.00        8988.00       -1.74\par  Rupee            39.75          44.26      +11.33\par  Ringgit         3.4115         3.5270       +3.39\par  Yuan            7.5112         7.8051       +3.91\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ASIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|IF|PHD|SI|Z|J|SNS|SNI|RNP|DNP|PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020071001e39s0007x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
